{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_011Ch3needm57ZtLTijTJwWh","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `wholsale` to `wholesale` in the October and November files and committed both in one commit, `63f572f`. `scripts/check.sh` passed first. I didn't fix December in the commit, and the single commit has an import problem you should know about.\n\n- **Import problem:** the README says the nightly import reloads only the data file for the month in the commit message's prefix. I used `2025-11:`, so November will reload with the fix and October won't. If the import has to pick up October as well, it needs its own commit prefixed `2025-10:`. That would mean two commits instead of the one you can revert in one go. Tell me if you want me to split it.\n- **December:** there is no `data/2025-12.csv`. The December request from earlier was never completed. The only December file is `inbox/2025-12.csv`, which is gitignored. I corrected the typo there too, so it's fixed once that file is added. That change is uncommitted and not part of `63f572f`.\n- **Nothing else:** no other file in the repo contains the typo.","citations":[]}],"model":"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":329,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":210,"cache_read_input_tokens":19931,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":210,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":"standard","speed":"standard"},"provider":"Anthropic","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<uuid-1>","uuid":"<uuid-48>","timestamp":"2026-11-15T00:44:13.296Z","request_id":"gen-1794703449-L2nGmiKHqmpZMmvrkGcz"}
